{"text": "38:34 :{c]454 PRODUCT SPECIFICATIONS\n\nBERGER GLOSS 7\n\nAlkyd Enamel Finish\n\nPRODUCT A solvent-based quality alkyd coating formulated with weather resistant inert pigments that\nDESCRIPTION provides an attractive and durable finish.\n> Good outdoor durability and colour retention properties.\n> Excellent adhesion to ferrous surfaces, wood and aged coatings.\n> Suitable for application as a finish coat for masonry substrates.\n> Easy application by brush or roller.\n> High opacity / covering ability.\n> Lead and Chrome free.\n> Washable and able to clean to keep away from dirt pickup.\n\nVv\n\nCertified for compliance to SS7 by TUV SUD PSB Pte Ltd.\n\nDESIGN > Asa finish coat for both interior and exterior ferrous surfaces, masonry substrates, wood\nUSE and timber products etc.\n> Asamaintenance coating over aged coatings.\n\nPHYSICAL DATA VOLUME SOLIDS 50%\nDRY FILM THICKNESS (DFT) 25-35 um per coat\nWET FILM THICKNESS (WFT) 50-70 um per coat\n\nNUMBER OF COATS 2\nTHEORETICAL COVERAGE 20.0 m\u00e9Jlitre per coat @ 25 yum dft\nFINISH Gloss, Semi-gloss & Matt\nCOLOUR RANGE Wide range available. (Please refer to our colour fan deck)\nNO. OF COMPONENTS One\n\nSTANDARD PACKING SIZE 5 Litres\n\nAPPLICATION Brush, Roller or These are the recommended methods of application.\nMETHOD Conventional Air Spray\nStir contents of the can thoroughly before use. Thinning is not usually required. However, if\nthinning is desired, do not exceed the recommended thinning ratio.\nDo not apply this product if the relative humidity exceeds 85% or if the substrate temperature is\n\nwithin 3\u00b0C of the dew point.\nDRYING TIME Substrate Touch Dry Hard Dry Overcoating Interval\nTemperature Minimum Maximum\n15 \u00b0C 12 hours 24 hours 16 hours Indefinite\n25 \u00b0C 6 hours 16 hours 12 hours Indefinite\n35 \u00b0C 3 hours 12 hours 6 hours Indefinite\nADDITIONAL Thinner Solvalux 7-9\nINFORMATION Thinning Ratio 5% maximum\nCleaning Solvent Solvalux 7-9\nFlash Point > 38\u00b0C\nStorage Requirements Store in a cool, dry area away from direct sunlight.\nBERGER GLOSS 7 REVISION 6/ 2014\n\nS1",
